          "english": "This is where a lot of people have trouble. Once upon a time, it was just customary for a bride to take her groom's last name as her own and abandon her maiden name completely. The act of keeping her own last name was considered taboo(禁忌) and people's eyebrows would raise right off their faces when they found out that the bride was even considering something so radical. Over time, though, more and more women are deciding to keep their last names.",
          "chinese": "这就是很多人感到困扰的地方。曾几何时，新娘采用新郎的姓氏作为自己的姓氏并完全放弃娘家姓只是一种习俗。保留自己姓氏的做法被认为是禁忌，当人们发现新娘甚至在考虑如此激进的事情时，会大为吃惊。然而随着时间推移，越来越多的女性决定保留自己的姓氏。",
